    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="12" relname="circumstance">According to your thread, you want us to refer to the HCI Bibliography and reference the Preece's book.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="13" relname="span">While doing this I was thinking of userablity, affordablity, visiabilty and etc....</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="14" relname="span">At the same time I was thinking this is a difficult thread to crunch in our brains;</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="16" relname="span">do to the fact that the Internet is still in its infancy staige.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="17" relname="span">Tomorrow's Internet may completely link with a human's thought process and be able to communicate based on the synapses of our brains.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="7" relname="concession">Yes, this is a bizarre thought</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="18" relname="span">however the electricity was considered strange too.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="16" relname="elaboration">In my opinion, technology will ever become more human interactive, as simple as talking to your friend.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="19" relname="span">The guidelines I have read thus far are so general</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="9" relname="elaboration">they in themselves are adaptive.</segment>
